This, and other window-related changes. What for?
I wager it's some sort of bug fix that was particularly necessary in this PR in order to respect the property hints everywhere. Previously this went unnoticed because the default `PROPERTY_HINT_RANGE` is almost inconsequential.

Either way, I think this can be rewritten this way (not tested)? Sure would be nice to have interfaces right now...

```suggestion
	if (checkable && !checked) {
		Control *control = Object::cast_to<Control>(object);
		if (control && String(property).begins_with("theme_override_")) {
			return control->get_used_theme_item(property);
		}
		Window *wnd = Object::cast_to<Window>(object);
		if (wnd && String(property).begins_with("theme_override_")) {
			return wnd->get_used_theme_item(property);
		}
	}
	return get_edited_property_value();
